x86_64-linux  every constructor and destructor here is implicit or defined inside its class, and clang then emits only the C2 and D2 variants on this target where cxx1 emits C1 and C2 - the difference move-constructor.nonames records.
x86_64-windows  clang writes a second base class descriptor for A, ??_R1A@?0A@EN@A@@8, attributes 0x4d, for A reached through a private base, where cxx1 uses the public one for every path - the Microsoft RTTI of a non-public base, not written yet (CLAUDE.md, "A non-public base is accessible where [class.access.base]/4 says"). arm64-darwin agrees name for name.
